\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Multiplication must bring the coefficients together}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A scalar vertex value can multiply a matter value in the
same fiber. Consider an edge cochain based at the initial vertex and a
vertex cochain evaluated at the terminal vertex. Their
coefficients can then lie in different fibers. Which transport brings the
two values into a common fiber, and in which module should their
product lie when the coefficient module has no multiplication?}
